+## VECTORIZED IMPLEMENTATION PATTERN (USE THIS TO AVOID TIMEOUTS)
+If implementing JADE/SHADE-style mutation, DO NOT write per-individual Python loops. Instead, generate all mutant vectors as a NumPy array:
+
+```python
+# Vectorized current-to-pbest/1 mutation for the whole population:
+sorted_idx = np.argsort(fitness)
+pbest_indices = sorted_idx[rng.randint(0, max(1, int(pop_size * p)), size=pop_size)]
+r1 = rng.randint(0, pop_size, size=pop_size)
+r2 = rng.randint(0, pop_size + len(archive), size=pop_size)
+r2_archive = r2 >= pop_size
+x_r2 = np.where(r2_archive, archive[r2 - pop_size], pop[r2])  # if archive is a 2D array
+F_i = np.clip(mu_F + 0.1 * rng.standard_cauchy(pop_size), 0.1, 1.0)
+CR_i = np.clip(mu_CR + 0.1 * rng.randn(pop_size), 0.0, 1.0)
+mutants = pop + F_i[:, None] * (pop[pbest_indices] - pop) + F_i[:, None] * (pop[r1] - x_r2)
+mask = rng.rand(pop_size, self.dim) < CR_i[:, None]
+j_rand = rng.randint(0, self.dim, size=pop_size)
+mask[np.arange(pop_size), j_rand] = True
+trials = np.where(mask, mutants, pop)
+# then evaluate trials and do selection (still vectorizable)
+```
